  "body": "From: Tyler Benson <tyler.benson@redwoodinference.com>\nTo: Paula Mendes <paula.mendes@redwoodinference.com>, Logan Wright <logan.wright@redwoodinference.com>\nCc: Ben Carter <ben.carter@redwoodinference.com>, Jada Williams <jada.williams@redwoodinference.com>\nDate: Mon, Jan 6, 2025 at 9:12 AM PT\nSubject: Activation sprint: UTM conventions + mapping campaign clicks to product events\n\nHey all \u2014 I\u2019m setting up the attribution conventions for the lifecycle growth sprint and want to lock two things this week:\n\n1) UTM conventions (naming + required params) for:\n- Onboarding email series\n- In-console CTAs that route to docs/quickstarts\n- Retargeting (LinkedIn/Google)\n\n2) How campaign clicks map into product events so we can answer \u201cwhich touch drove activation\u201d without guesswork.\n\nProposal (happy to adjust):\n- Require UTMs on all outbound links from campaigns: utm_source, utm_medium, utm_campaign, utm_content (optional), utm_term (optional)\n- Also capture click ids when present: gclid (Google), li_fat_id (LinkedIn)\n- Persist on first landing (cookie/localStorage) for 30d; attach to product events for the first 7d after signup (or until activation) to keep noise down.\n\nQuestions to align on:\n- Which product events should carry campaign properties? (My guess: sign_up_completed, api_key_created, first_request_success, first_streaming_success, dashboard_viewed, billing_added)\n- For activation reporting, do we want last-touch (most recent click before activation) or first-touch (first campaign touch)?\n- Any schema constraints on property names / cardinality (Logan)?\n- Any privacy/consent constraints we should reflect (Paula \u2014 I saw the marketing tracking review doc, but want to be sure we\u2019re aligned)?\n\nIf we can converge by Wed, I\u2019ll update the shared conventions doc and we can unblock ENG-2844.\n\nThanks,\nTyler\n\n\u2014\nTyler Benson\nMarketing Ops & Attribution\nRedwood Inference\n\n\nFrom: Paula Mendes <paula.mendes@redwoodinference.com>\nTo: Tyler Benson <tyler.benson@redwoodinference.com>\nCc: Logan Wright <logan.wright@redwoodinference.com>, Ben Carter <ben.carter@redwoodinference.com>, Jada Williams <jada.williams@redwoodinference.com>\nDate: Mon, Jan 6, 2025 at 12:04 PM PT\nSubject: Re: Activation sprint: UTM conventions + mapping campaign clicks to product events\n\nTyler \u2014 yes to locking this week.\n\nTelemetry POV:\n- We should attach campaign properties to events that define the funnel steps, not every event (otherwise we\u2019ll inflate payloads and increase cardinality).\n- For this sprint, we can focus on:\n  - api_key_created\n  - first_request_success (first 2xx completion)\n  - first_streaming_success\n  - dashboard_viewed (cost/latency dashboard)\n  - billing_added\n\nPersistence:\n- Agree on persisting UTMs on landing.\n- We should also handle the \u201cemail click -> console -> user signs up\u201d path. If the user lands on console unauthenticated, we need UTMs to survive through auth redirect.\n\nAttribution model:\n- For sprint readout, we probably want both:\n  - last_touch_before_activation\n  - first_touch_in_window\n\nPrivacy:\n- Keep the captured fields limited to UTM + click ids. No new PII.\n- Anything stored beyond standard retention should be covered by the marketing tracking review; as long as we use existing retention + honor unsubscribe/suppression we\u2019re good. (Main caution: don\u2019t attach raw full URL querystrings, only whitelisted params.)\n\nPaula\n\n\nFrom: Logan Wright <logan.wright@redwoodinference.com>\nTo: Tyler Benson <tyler.benson@redwoodinference.com>\nCc: Paula Mendes <paula.mendes@redwoodinference.com>, Ben Carter <ben.carter@redwoodinference.com>, Jada Williams <jada.williams@redwoodinference.com>\nDate: Tue, Jan 7, 2025 at 8:46 AM PT\nSubject: Re: Activation sprint: UTM conventions + mapping campaign clicks to product events\n\n+1 to Paula\u2019s list.\n\nSchema notes / constraints:\n- Please use our reserved naming convention for marketing props:\n  - marketing_utm_source\n  - marketing_utm_medium\n  - marketing_utm_campaign\n  - marketing_utm_content\n  - marketing_utm_term\n  - marketing_gclid\n  - marketing_li_fat_id\n- Avoid arbitrary \u201ccampaign_name\u201d strings outside utm_campaign \u2014 it creates inconsistencies.\n- Cardinality: utm_campaign can still explode if folks put free-form text. Strongly recommend a structured pattern (e.g., lc_sprint_welcome_v1) and a separate spreadsheet lookup for human-readable labels.\n\nAlso: we should log a derived boolean like marketing_attributed=true when we have any whitelisted param present. This helps keep queries simple.\n\nIf ENG-2844 is implementing a client+server join, we should define precedence when multiple touches exist. My vote: store last touch in session + also keep first touch (in a separate \u201c*_first\u201d set) so analysis doesn\u2019t require event stitching gymnastics.\n\nLogan\n\n\nFrom: Ben Carter <ben.carter@redwoodinference.com>\nTo: Tyler Benson <tyler.benson@redwoodinference.com>\nCc: Paula Mendes <paula.mendes@redwoodinference.com>, Logan Wright <logan.wright@redwoodinference.com>, Jada Williams <jada.williams@redwoodinference.com>\nDate: Tue, Jan 7, 2025 at 10:15 AM PT\nSubject: Re: Activation sprint: UTM conventions + mapping campaign clicks to product events\n\nThis is great.\n\nTwo requests from Growth:\n1) Can we make the campaign naming pattern idiot-proof for the email series? We\u2019ll have variants and need to compare apples-to-apples.\n   - e.g., utm_campaign=lc_onboarding_welcome_v1\n   - utm_content=subjectA vs subjectB (or variantA/variantB)\n\n2) For retargeting, we\u2019ll need a clear way to split:\n   - non_activated_signup (no first_request_success within 72h)\n   - lapsed (had success before, but 14d inactivity)\n\nIf you can propose the exact required fields + an example for each channel, I\u2019ll bake into the launch checklist.\n\nBen\n\n\nFrom: Tyler Benson <tyler.benson@redwoodinference.com>\nTo: Ben Carter <ben.carter@redwoodinference.com>, Paula Mendes <paula.mendes@redwoodinference.com>, Logan Wright <logan.wright@redwoodinference.com>, Jada Williams <jada.williams@redwoodinference.com>\nDate: Wed, Jan 8, 2025 at 3:22 PM PT\nSubject: Re: Activation sprint: UTM conventions + mapping campaign clicks to product events\n\nAwesome \u2014 incorporated all feedback.\n\nAttached: UTM_Conventions_ActivationSprint_v1.xlsx\n\nWhat\u2019s in the sheet:\n- Required params by channel (email, retargeting, in-console docs CTAs)\n- Naming pattern + allowed values (to keep utm_campaign low-cardinality)\n- Example URLs for each campaign\n- A \u201chuman label\u201d column so we don\u2019t overload utm_campaign with prose\n\nTL;DR conventions:\n- utm_campaign pattern:\n  - lc_<surface>_<audience>_<message>_v<##>\n  - examples:\n    - lc_email_newsignup_welcome_v01\n    - lc_email_newsignup_firstsuccess_v01\n    - lc_li_nonactivated_benchmarks_v01\n    - lc_google_lapsed_troubleshoot_v01\n- utm_content = variant or creative id (e.g., subjectA, banner_copyB, creative03)\n- utm_source allowed values: email | linkedin | google | console\n- utm_medium allowed values: lifecycle | retargeting | nudge\n\nEvent mapping proposal (aligning to Paula/Logan):\n- Add whitelisted marketing_* props to:\n  - api_key_created\n  - first_request_success\n  - first_streaming_success\n  - dashboard_viewed\n  - billing_added\n- Capture on landing, persist 30d; attach to events for 7d post-signup OR until first_request_success (whichever comes first) so we don\u2019t attribute long-tail behavior to an initial click.\n\nEngineering note:\n- If we can implement first-touch + last-touch fields (as Logan suggested), that\u2019d be ideal:\n  - marketing_utm_campaign_first / _last, etc.\n\nAlso attaching a short text note with property whitelist + precedence rules for ENG.\n\nAttachment stubs:\n- UTM_Conventions_ActivationSprint_v1.xlsx\n- Attribution_Event_Mapping_Notes.txt\n\nJada \u2014 does this match what you\u2019re expecting to implement under ENG-2844? If yes, I\u2019ll update the GTM conventions doc and the experiment tracker fields.\n\nTyler\n\n\nFrom: Jada Williams <jada.williams@redwoodinference.com>\nTo: Tyler Benson <tyler.benson@redwoodinference.com>\nCc: Ben Carter <ben.carter@redwoodinference.com>, Paula Mendes <paula.mendes@redwoodinference.com>, Logan Wright <logan.wright@redwoodinference.com>\nDate: Thu, Jan 9, 2025 at 4:37 PM PT\nSubject: Re: Activation sprint: UTM conventions + mapping campaign clicks to product events\n\nYes \u2014 this lines up with ENG-2844.\n\nImplementation plan (so you know what will/won\u2019t be true for v1):\n- We\u2019ll capture whitelisted params client-side on initial landing and store:\n  - first-touch set (immutable)\n  - last-touch set (updated on subsequent landings)\n- We\u2019ll propagate the last-touch set into event props for the funnel events Paula listed.\n- For auth redirect: we\u2019ll pass the whitelisted props through the redirect state so they survive from /console -> /auth -> back.\n\nTwo edge cases we may not nail in week 0:\n- Cross-device (email opened on mobile, later signup on desktop) \u2014 we won\u2019t stitch without identity.\n- Cookie-disabled browsers \u2014 we\u2019ll still have UTMs on the landing page view event, but not guaranteed on later events.\n\nIf you\u2019re good with those limitations, we\u2019re unblocked.\n\nJada"
